, while others in the same list carry a tag because their author typed one. The format is read from the file name, so the list stops being half-labelled. No link text changes.","value":"43 links"},{"id":"emailchip","on":true,"label":"Make a loose address look like an address","why":"19 email addresses sit in the body of this page rather than in a contact block, drawn exactly like every other link — so the one that opens a mail window looks the same as the ones that go to web pages. The chip carries the same envelope the banner's contact link uses. The address itself does not change.","value":"19 addresses"},{"id":"deck","on":true,"label":"Use this paragraph as the page description","why":"It is the page’s own opening paragraph, moved into the banner rather than rewritten.","value":"Welcome to the Maine Department of Education professional learning webinar library. Here you can find a series of recorded webinars and training across a broad scope of topic areas shared by Maine DOE staff and endorsed partners."},{"id":"banner-graphic","on":true,"label":"Retire the old banner graphic","why":"It repeats the page title in picture form, which the new banner already does in type.","removes":"Professional Webinar Library Web Banner.png"},{"id":"searchtable","on":true,"label":"Let a long table be searched","why":"1 table runs to fifteen rows or more, so finding one row means reading every row. The theme already loads the search behaviour on every page and switches it on for any table marked this way — 26 tables across the site already are, including the contact directory. It adds a search box, a length menu and a pager, and makes the column headings sortable; ten rows show at a time, which is the library's own default. Nothing is reordered until someone asks.","value":"1 table"}],"mechanical":["drupal entity attrs stripped: 2","target set by destination: 45","loose text wrapped in a paragraph: 42","paragraph inside a table cell unwrapped: 43","tables normalised to the house s